  "survive": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "why": "two equal, well-formed digests that are not this run's: the sha256 of the empty string, in both. Not pinned by choice: the bytes depend on the inference build, and the owner's ruling \"apr version is 0.70.*\" leaves the patch version free, so pinning a digest would pin the patch",
      "rust_assert": "the program recomputes sha256 over out/answers.json ‖ out/verdicts.json after each schedule and asserts it equals the recorded digest",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/digest_sequential",
          "value": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/digest_pipelined",
          "value": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "why": "two equal, plausible pids that are not this server's: 41388 in both. pid 0 and 1 are refused by a pattern on both fields, so this row uses a pid the shapes cannot tell apart",
      "rust_assert": "the pid is read from the spawned child handle, and /proc/<pid>/exe must resolve to the apr binary whose sha256 the Receipt records",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/server_pid_start",
          "value": 41388
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/server_pid_end",
          "value": 41388
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "why": "one decision flipped, q3 reject to accept. Not pinned by choice: decisions depend on the inference build, which the owner's ruling \"apr version is 0.70.*\" leaves free across patch versions",
      "rust_assert": "decisions are parsed from out/verdicts.json, the file only the checker wrote, and both digests cover that file",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q3/decision",
          "value": "accept"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "why": "one item shifted 100 s later, all eight of its timestamps alike, so q2 now follows q3",
      "rust_assert": "every timestamp comes from one monotonic clock at the sink; items are increasing in i within a schedule and each is at most that schedule's elapsed time",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/seq_writer_start_ms",
          "value": 102281
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/seq_writer_end_ms",
          "value": 103460
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/seq_checker_start_ms",
          "value": 103461
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/seq_checker_end_ms",
          "value": 104570
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/pipe_writer_start_ms",
          "value": 101177
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/pipe_writer_end_ms",
          "value": 103390
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/pipe_checker_start_ms",
          "value": 103391
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/pipe_checker_end_ms",
          "value": 104520
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "why": "writer_files lists out/answers.json twice: an equivalent mutant, since RDF values are a set",
      "rust_assert": "each role sink opens its file with create_new, so a second open of one path is an error, not a second entry",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "add",
          "path": "/writer_files/-",
          "value": "out/answers.json"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "why": "a pipelined schedule that never overlapped: each writer starts only after the previous item's checker ended, so it is a sequential run under the pipelined label. Every per-item chain is still ordered",
      "rust_assert": "for i in 1..3, pipe_writer_start(q(i+1)) < pipe_checker_end(q(i)): the writer of the next item started while the checker of this one was still running",
      "patch": [
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q2/pipe_writer_start_ms",
          "value": 2301
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
          "path": "/q3/pipe_writer_start_ms",
          "value": 4521
        },
        {
          "op": "replace",
